<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) LOWERS GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) LOWERS GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will lower gasoline prices by 0.30 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport diesel and heating fuel prices will remain unchanged, it said.</p>
<p>The price adjustment comes after lower world gasoline prices, down $1.6 per metric tonne, along with a fairly stable world diesel price and dollar/drachma exchange rate, DEP said.</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
